From a74b0dcd79572bf6609f34ed0b8ca3e0bcf12404 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koshindai <97556702+Koshindai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:22:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: an App icon tab chooses the icon of the built app

The artwork panel gets a third tab. It offers the game's own icon (when
the last build's extraction still has it), the eShop icon (downloaded
on demand) and the player's own square images, with Dock and iPhone
previews of the choice. The library dims while it is open, since it
does not show the icon.

A build passes the chosen icon to the engine as DM_ICON, for the IPA
and the Mac app alike. The game's own icon, or a file that is gone,
leaves it unset. After saving a new icon for a game already built, the
hero says "New app icon at the next build" beside the Rebuild capsule,
until the game is rebuilt or another game is selected.

Depends on the DM_ICON patch (0034).
